// @run
// @log 7
// D311's NAMED SET — the 5 cells the close MOVES plus the 1 that already ran
// (silent-class-inventory D311, the fourth end of D209's channel).
//
// WHY THESE ARE A NAMED SET AND NOT A DERIVED ONE. On the closing compiler all six of these
// RUN and print `7`, exactly like thousands of their neighbours, so nothing reading current
// behaviour can separate them. What makes them worth keeping is the ABLATION: without rung S
// (`memberUnionReadKind` answering the channel's delivered atom) three go check-clean invalid
// wasm; without rung N (`unionNameOfExpr` declining a channel-unboxed read) two more do; and
// the sixth is the CONTROL that separates the axis and must never move in either direction.
// The census's own population cannot carry them either — block A pins the payload at `7`, so
// its `stri32` coordinate never exercises the string atom this family is silent at.
//
// CELL 3 — the LOCAL rebind. Rung S alone is NOT enough here: it makes the binding's slot a
// string ref (`letIsString` reads the init through `exprString`) while `unionNameOfExpr`
// still registers the binding as a UNION one, and `unionIdentReadKind` then overrides
// `exprString` at the print. Needs S AND N — this cell is why N is in the commit.
type Circle = { r: string | i32 }
const v = { r: "7" }
const z = (v).r
print(z)
